From: David Bau <davidbau@csail.mit.edu>
Date: 2026-06-19
Subject: [PATCH] doborn: emit the totals row that Sprintf already builds

`doborn()` formats a totals row into `buf` via Sprintf at the end of
its per-PM loop, then immediately calls `display_nhwindow` without a
matching `putstr` — so the buffer is computed and abandoned, and the
displayed `#wizborn` window is missing its summary row.

The per-PM loop above uses the same fmt template with a matching
Sprintf/putstr pair, the empty-separator `putstr` directly above the
trailing Sprintf only has visual purpose if a totals row was meant
to follow, and Sprintf with no consumer has no other rationale. The
most parsimonious explanation is a missed `putstr` call.

Fix: insert the missing `putstr(datawin, 0, buf);` between the
Sprintf and the display_nhwindow.

---
 src/insight.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/insight.c b/src/insight.c
index 0000000..0000001 100644
--- a/src/insight.c
+++ b/src/insight.c
@@ -3167,6 +3167,7 @@ doborn(void)

     putstr(datawin, 0, "");
     Sprintf(buf, fmt, ndied, nborn, ' ', "");
+    putstr(datawin, 0, buf);

     display_nhwindow(datawin, FALSE);
     destroy_nhwindow(datawin);
